          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              A generalization of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+de+Rham+theorem"} equivariant de Rham theorem
              to non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact
              Lie groups exists (
              %a{:href => "#Getzler94"}> Getzler 94
              ) but this uses the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+de+Rham+complex"} simplicial de Rham complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \sslash G
              (
              %a{:href => "#BottShulmanStasheff76"}> Bott-Shulman-Stasheff 76
              ) and is thus a fair bit more complicated, computationally.
          %h3#CartanMap Cartan’s map
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-space"} G-manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = P
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to B
            %em Cartan map
            (or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan%27s+map"} Cartan's map
            or similar) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+model"} Cartan model
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+de+Rham+cohomology"} equivariant de Rham cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = P
            to the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            model for the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            of the base manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
